B.U2=new A.j1("Research","1. Company proof \u2014 account fits the ICP.\n2. Role proof \u2014 contact has plausible responsibility.\n3. Contact proof \u2014 legitimate route exists; never guess.\n4. Reason proof \u2014 account-specific relevance supported by evidence.","Four-Proof Lead Check")
B.U0=new A.j1("Outreach","Observation: one verified reason this company is relevant.\nRelevance: why that may matter.\nCapability: what you can honestly help with.\nAsk: one low-friction next step.\n\nDo not fake familiarity or invent a problem.","Cold Outreach Skeleton")
B.U_=new A.j1("Calling","1. Acknowledge what they actually said.\n2. Answer the question if you can.\n3. If you cannot, say so clearly.\n4. Ask one relevant question.\n5. Return to the next useful step\u2014not blindly to the script.","Off-Script Recovery")
B.U1=new A.j1("Discovery","Before the call: what they sell, who they sell to, likely sales motion, one verified observation, three priority questions, one useful artifact, and the desired next step.","Discovery Prep")
B.U4=new A.j1("Conversion","Problem \u2192 objective \u2192 bounded scope \u2192 deliverables \u2192 client responsibilities \u2192 process/funnel metrics \u2192 duration \u2192 compensation \u2192 review point.\n\nNever guarantee outcomes outside your control.","Paid Pilot Frame")
B.TZ=new A.j1("Metrics","Track accounts researched, prospects added, touches, follow-ups, replies, positive interest, qualified opportunities, meetings booked/held, objections, one experiment, and next actions.","Weekly Review")
B.TX=new A.j1("Pipeline","Company \xb7 website \xb7 lane \xb7 contact \xb7 role \xb7 contact route \xb7 fit score \xb7 priority \xb7 status \xb7 first touch \xb7 last touch \xb7 next action \xb7 next-action date \xb7 source URL \xb7 reply/outcome \xb7 notes.","Acquisition Tracker Fields")
B.U3=new A.j1("Delivery","Commercial: scope, compensation, payment timing, duration.\nOffer/market: product, ICP, exclusions, geography, target roles, qualification rule.\nBoundaries: approved claims, pricing/technical escalation, authority limits.\nTools: CRM, dialer, email, calendar, lead source, reporting location.\nWorkflow: daily expectation, follow-up cadence, handoff, reporting, response-time expectations.","Client Onboarding Checklist")
